# R503 / R503-M22 Optical Fingerprint Module, The Realization Below The HAL [SPEC:CXC-R503]

> Everything in this document lives BELOW the seam: it binds the r503 driver and the R503
> realization of the HAL, and nothing above them. Hardware truths are preserved tightly;
> every inference is labelled as one; every hardware-observable claim has an empty evidence
> slot recording that no R503 has ever been on a bench in this project.

---

## Source and part identity

### [CXC-R503-SOURCE] The primary source is pinned by hash

- primary-source: R503_R503-M22_user_manual_V1.4.1_2023-09.pdf
- primary-source-sha256: fa5d4105f6754ddf0ebcbdb5875a78106a4f147534c3c3bbc0385bc5477dfc22
- citation-convention: p.N is the printed folio of V1.4.1; comparison revisions are V1.1, V1.2.1, V1.4, plus the R503-5V, R503S and R503Pro manuals as cross-part context.
- rule: every datasheet claim in this document is checkable against a named byte sequence. A claim that cannot cite a folio does not belong here.
- status: draft
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-R503]

### [CXC-R503-PART] The part

- interface: UART, 3.3 V TTL, default 57600 baud (p.1).
- capacity: 200 templates, consistent across all four revisions.
- template-size: 1536 bytes from V1.2.1 onward; V1.1 says 768. The size is announced by the HAL, never compiled in as a constant, because the parts in hand may run V1.1-era firmware ([CXC-FPHAL-CAPABILITIES-SCHEMA]).
- on-chip-matcher: the module performs 1:1 match and 1:N search itself, which is what made sensor-side matching available ([DD-R503-MATCH-LOCALITY]).
- accuracy-figures: FAR under 0.001 percent and FRR under 1 percent, published with no measurement conditions in any revision. Unfalsifiable; they upgrade nothing ([CXC-R503-ASSURANCE]).
- ring: a 7-colour, 6-mode addressable ring — [CXC-R503-AURA-LED].
- status: draft
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-R503]

### [CXC-R503-PART-IDENTITY] Which SKU is physically in hand

- question-state: PARTIAL
- hazard: four parts are sold as R503-something and listings conflate them. The R503-5V puts DC 5V on pin 1; applying this document's rail figures to it destroys the part.
- answered-2026-08-16: David — the parts in hand are 3.3 V, so the R503-5V is excluded. No serial or part number appears on any module, so R503 versus R503S versus R503Pro is open on paper.
- the-circularity-is-broken: knowing the rail is 3.3 V means the part can be safely powered and then ASKED what it is — ReadProdInfo 0x3C returns a 16-byte model string. The SKU stops being a precondition of bring-up and becomes its first measurement.
- consequence: every figure in this document is provisional until [CXC-R503-EV-02] returns a model string.
- status: draft
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-R503]

