## Timing

### [CXC-R503-TIMING] What is stated, what is absent, and where the cost lives

- stated: boot to ready about 50 ms; image acquisition under 0.2 s; feature generation under 500 ms; touch response about 120 ms; power-cycle dwell 2 s; ring animator minimum 5 s cycle.
- absent: no per-command latency table exists. GenChar, Match, Search, RegModel, Store, LoadChar, UpChar and DownChar have no figure; template-path timeouts are invented by the driver and must carry deadlines ([CXC-FPHAL-CONTAINMENT-INVARIANTS] inv-1).
- capture-dominates: a one-shot verify budget is roughly GetImg + GenChar + Search, about 0.71 s optimistic and 0.9 s pessimistic at a twenty-template cast — dominated by imaging, not matching. INFERENCE: arithmetic on separately-specified worst cases, an order-of-magnitude expectation and not a budget.
- match-time-string: the intro table's 1:N under 10 ms per fingerprint is ambiguous by a factor of 200 and is never restated. At the fleet's twenty-template cast both readings land inside a comfortable single-press interaction, so the ambiguity no longer decides any architecture; [CXC-R503-EV-09] measures it as an understanding check that gates nothing.
- status: draft
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-R503]

