## Cross-revision drift

### [CXC-R503-REVISION-DRIFT] The changelog is materially incomplete

- rule: do not use the vendor changelog to decide whether a revision matters. It records none of the physically consequential changes below.
- drift-connector: MX1.0--6P in three revisions, SH1.0--6P in V1.4.1.
- drift-electrical: 3.3VT range narrowed from 3-6 V to 3-5 V; the big-endian note, the dwell, and the touch figures all appear only from V1.2.1.
- drift-sizes: template 768 to 1536 bytes, characteristic 384 to 512 (V1.1 to V1.2.1) — load-bearing because the parts in hand may run V1.1-era firmware, which is why template size is announced rather than compiled in.
- drift-led: three ring colours in V1.1, seven from V1.2.1 — see the risk recorded at [CXC-R503-RING-REALIZATION].
- drift-behaviour: default security level 5 in three revisions, 3 in V1.4.1; system identifier code changed; AutoEnroll and AutoIdentify are absent from V1.1 entirely.
- status: draft
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-R503]

