## The ring

### [CXC-R503-AURA-LED] The ring LED

- command: AuraLedConfig 0x35, payload control, speed, colour index, times (p.27).
- modes: breathing, flashing, always on, always off, gradually on, gradually off.
- colours: SEVEN — red 0x01, blue 0x02, purple 0x03, green 0x04, yellow 0x05, cyan 0x06, white 0x07. A three-colour driver is a stale-V1.1 artifact and loses four.
- animator-floor: minimum 5 s animation cycle. Any sub-second feedback MUST be realized as always-on and always-off transitions timed by the host, never by the module's animator. A realization reaching for breathing to signal a 300 ms accept produces a five-second smear.
- status: draft
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-R503]

### [CXC-R503-RING-REALIZATION] The semantic-state realization table

- what-this-is: the R503-side realization of the semantic feedback states named at [CXC-FPID-FEEDBACK-STATES]. Colours are normative HERE and nowhere above the seam.
- rule-ready: ready renders blue 0x02 or purple 0x03 — David's stated preference, deliberately against the obvious green. A builder defaulting ready to green has violated the one UX preference he stated.
- rule-accept: accept renders green 0x04, always on, host-timed dwell.
- rule-rejections: both denial flavours render red 0x01. Which flavour a device shows is the game's choice and is not decided here.
- rule-reject-silent-duplicate-row: reject_silent and a genuine no_match are the SAME ROW — same colour, mode, speed, duration and command bytes, written as two rows with identical right-hand sides on purpose so any future divergence is visible as an edit. This is [CXC-FPID-REJECT-SILENT-RENDERING] binding on the one table it was always about.
- risk-green-may-not-exist: David's parts may run V1.1-era firmware, and V1.1 documents only red, blue and purple. Green first appears in V1.2.1. If green is absent the accept row needs a RULING, not a workaround — every remaining option collides with ready or runs into the animator floor. [CXC-R503-EV-11] settles it in about ten seconds and is the first thing to run.
- states-unmapped: idle, awaiting_finger, capture_accepted, capture_retry, enroll_progress, busy and fault have no colour assigned. Assigning them is a game-design call, deliberately not taken here.
- who-issues: the DEVICE, always. The driver renders a commanded state and originates none — [CXC-FPID-RING-OWNER].
- acceptance-human: GLASS GATE — every commanded state visibly distinct on a real ring EXCEPT the reject_silent and no_match pair, which must be visibly identical. No machine signal can stand in for this.
- status: draft
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-R503]

