## Platform binding

### [CXC-R503-HAL-BINDING] The declaration

- declaration: id bioscan, role transactional, driver r503, interface uart at 57600 baud, assurance experiential — canonical in platform spec 32 and inherited verbatim.
- namespace-literals: contested three ways across platform specs 27 and 32 and this corpus — [DD-R503-NAMESPACE-SPELLING]. Every topic literal in C73 is provisional until that is ruled.
- status: draft
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-R503]

### [CXC-R503-DEVICE-FACES] Two faces, one artifact

- runtime-face: a finger arrives, the module captures and searches, the driver reports a slot. One value, one event, no state beyond the read.
- management-face: enrollment and template transfer — stateful, multi-step, multi-second, with a human in the middle.
- consequence: one driver with two internally-distinct paths, not two drivers. The resumable state machine exists for the management face only.
- status: draft
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-R503]

### [CXC-R503-DRIVER-TIER] The driver is a bytecode-VM artifact with a CH32V203 floor

- tier: sandboxed bytecode VM. The part needs framing, checksums, timers, kilobyte buffers, resync and a multi-second human-interactive state machine — logic, not a data descriptor.
- floor: CH32V203. A CH32V003 cannot host it; a board intending an R503 on a V003 compiles the driver in or moves the peripheral to a capable peer.
- resumability: enrollment cannot block the tick loop; the driver's ceremony state machine advances one step per tick.
- current-host: the bring-up host is an ESP32-S3 SuperMini (David, 2026-08-16), far above the floor.
- status: draft
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-R503]

### [CXC-R503-ASSURANCE] The assurance class asserts a negative

- class: experiential — spoofable, no liveness detection, no secure element, NOT authentication and NOT access control. The name was questioned, ruled renamed, and the ruling reversed the same day; experiential stands (David, 2026-08-17).
- consequence: every match this part reports is theatrical. Latch fail-safe behaviour belongs to each integrating device's own declaration, as a required per-latch property with no default (David, 2026-08-17, per-hatch declaration; a mechanical release is not characterized at the software level).
- status: draft
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-R503]

### [CXC-R503-DRIVER-SURVEY] Six drivers surveyed; none is safe to adopt as-is

- best-structural-model: FPM — an explicit FSM parser, inter-byte timeouts, a self-resynchronising sliding header window, and transport failure numerically disjoint from sensor refusal.
- the-graft: take esphome's full RX drain before every transmit; lift esphome's complete LED enums; mine R503Lib for missing opcodes. Three licences are touched at once — confirm before any code ([CXC-R503-PRE-DRIVER-BASELINE]).
- safety-defects: R503Lib reads a wire-supplied length into a fixed stack array with no bounds check — a remote stack smash. pyfingerprint's read loop has no deadline — a silent module hangs the host forever. Both defects are the direct sources of containment invariants inv-1 and inv-2.
- licence-hazards: pyfingerprint is D-FSL, copyleft and non-OSI; esphome's vendored component has no determinable licence in-tree.
- conclusion: the driver cannot be a port. The stream path has no prior art anywhere and must be authored from the document and bench-verified.
- status: draft
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-R503]

