## Decisions

### [DD-R503-MATCH-LOCALITY] Matching is sensor-side

- decision: sensor-side matching. Architect's call 2026-08-15 on David's constraint of the same day, open to his dissent.
- the-collapsing-constraint: the fleet is at most ten identities times two fingers — twenty templates per device — so the pessimistic reading of the match-time ambiguity costs 200 ms, and sensor-side wins under both readings.
- rationale: the module owns capture, extraction, storage and matching; the leaf that can fully own the behaviour owns it, and it works with the bus down.
- invalidating_assumption: that a deployment has one cast shared by all readers. Many readers over disjoint populations would reopen this.
- status: draft
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-R503]

### [DD-R503-NAMESPACE-SPELLING] The namespace literals are contested and not settled here

- decision: NOT MADE. Platform specs 27 and 32 and this corpus spell the fingerprint surface three different ways, and picking one silently would leave the corpus disagreeing with itself.
- blocked-on: write access to the platform corpus; the amendment lands with the migration out of staging.
- interim-rule: every topic literal in C73 is structural, not literal — a builder takes the message SHAPES as normative and the spellings as provisional.
- status: draft
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-R503]

