## Post-integration evidence ledger

### [CXC-R503-EV-INDEX] The ledger — 0 of 12 slots filled

- slots-total: 12
- slots-filled: 0
- hardware-status: no R503 has ever been connected to anything in this project. Every slot below is EMPTY and says so; an unfilled slot carries an explicit EMPTY sentinel, never an absent key.
- destructive-tests-removed: the prior ledger's overdrive-RXD and baud-probe slots are DELETED. Both were brick-risk tests defending rules that stand without them: never assume 5 V tolerance, and never issue a baud change. No slot below can damage a module.
- fill-protocol: replace EMPTY with the observation, its date and its observer; leave the question and expectation untouched so prediction and outcome remain comparable.
- status: draft
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-R503]

### [CXC-R503-EV-01] Pin 1 by continuity, never by colour

- question: with the connector latch facing a known direction, meter continuity from each contact and confirm the order VCC, GND, TXD, RXD, WAKEUP, 3.3VT.
- expected: the six functions in that order, GND anchoring the count.
- discriminates: a reversed order means the photograph was read from the wrong face and every connection is mirrored.
- observed: EMPTY
- status: draft
- part-of: [CXC-R503-EV-INDEX]

### [CXC-R503-EV-02] Confirm the SKU and firmware version over the wire

- question: issue ReadProdInfo 0x3C and GetFwVer 0x3A; record the model string and firmware version.
- expected: a string identifying an R503 or R503-M22.
- discriminates: an R503S or R503Pro string means the cross-part context applies rather than the primary source; the firmware version decides whether the V1.1 three-colour and 768-byte-template era applies.
- observed: EMPTY
- status: draft
- part-of: [CXC-R503-EV-INDEX]

### [CXC-R503-EV-03] Scope WAKEUP's high level at 3.3VT = 3.3 V

- question: with 3.3VT tied to 3.3 V, scope WAKEUP's high level with VCC on and off.
- expected: a high tracking 3.3 V in both VCC states.
- discriminates: a high tracking VCC instead falsifies the rail inference and reopens the conditioning question.
- observed: EMPTY
- status: draft
- part-of: [CXC-R503-EV-INDEX]

### [CXC-R503-EV-04] Current in the three states the manual conflates

- question: measure supply current idle, during acquisition, and with the ring commanded full white always-on.
- expected: acquisition near 20 mA; the ring figure is unknown by construction.
- discriminates: a ring figure that pushes the total past the SuperMini LDO's comfortable margin reopens the shared-rail ruling with data rather than inference.
- observed: EMPTY
- status: draft
- part-of: [CXC-R503-EV-INDEX]

### [CXC-R503-EV-05] Capture the power-on 0x55

- question: capture the serial line from VCC rising and record the unsolicited byte and its timing.
- expected: a single bare 0x55 shortly after the roughly 50 ms init window.
- discriminates: absence, framing, or a different value changes the resync design.
- observed: EMPTY
- status: draft
- part-of: [CXC-R503-EV-INDEX]

### [CXC-R503-EV-06] Confirm 0x55 after SoftRst

- question: issue SoftRst 0x3D and capture whether 0x55 is re-emitted.
- expected: re-emission, per three manual statements.
- discriminates: no re-emission would make the boot-only handling sufficient after all; the drain-plus-window remedy stands either way.
- observed: EMPTY
- status: draft
- part-of: [CXC-R503-EV-INDEX]

### [CXC-R503-EV-07] Bound the AutoIdentify stream

- question: with retries 0 and a never-matching finger held on the sensor, count acknowledge packets over 60 seconds.
- expected: unbounded emission, per the inference.
- discriminates: a bounded stream shrinks the RX ring requirement; unbounded confirms the sizing hazard. Run with a matching finger as the control proving the command runs at all.
- observed: EMPTY
- status: draft
- part-of: [CXC-R503-EV-INDEX]

### [CXC-R503-EV-08] What happens to a command sent while Busy

- question: start a long operation, poll Busy, send a benign read command mid-operation, and record whether it is queued, rejected or dropped.
- expected: unknown by construction — the manual does not say.
- discriminates: queued means a simple pipeline; rejected means a retry policy; dropped means a Busy poll before every command.
- observed: EMPTY
- status: draft
- part-of: [CXC-R503-EV-INDEX]

### [CXC-R503-EV-09] Time a search at one and at twenty templates

- question: measure Search latency with one resident template and with twenty.
- expected: both readings of the match-time string predict under 200 ms at twenty.
- discriminates: settles which reading of 1:N under 10 ms per fingerprint is true; gates nothing. First prove twenty templates are genuinely resident, or the fast result measures an empty search.
- observed: EMPTY
- status: draft
- part-of: [CXC-R503-EV-INDEX]

### [CXC-R503-EV-10] Count ReadProdInfo's bytes on the wire

- question: issue ReadProdInfo 0x3C and count the data bytes.
- expected: 46 or 50 — the document contradicts itself by exactly four bytes.
- discriminates: which parser length is correct on shipped firmware.
- observed: EMPTY
- status: draft
- part-of: [CXC-R503-EV-INDEX]

### [CXC-R503-EV-11] Census the ring colours the firmware actually drives

- question: command each of the seven documented colours always-on in sequence and record which render.
- expected: seven distinct colours on V1.2.1-era firmware; possibly three on V1.1-era.
- discriminates: whether the accept-is-green row of the realization table is implementable on the parts in hand. Ten seconds of bench time; run first.
- observed: EMPTY
- status: draft
- part-of: [CXC-R503-EV-INDEX]

### [CXC-R503-EV-12] Negative control for the WAKEUP measurement

- question: with the same probe and setup as EV-03, confirm the finger-detect path actually fires — present a finger and observe the WAKEUP transition.
- expected: a clean high-to-low transition on finger contact.
- discriminates: proves the probe and the detect path both work, so a null result on EV-03 is a finding rather than a broken harness.
- observed: EMPTY
- status: draft
- part-of: [CXC-R503-EV-INDEX]

